WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.030
On the coast of County Antrim, about 40,000
basalt columns stand packed together:

2
00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:07.850
the Giant's Causeway.

3
00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:11.630
They formed about 50 to
60 million years ago.

4
00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:15.490
On Dartmoor, granite is full
of crystals you can see.

5
00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:19.710
In the Brecon Beacons, red
sandstone often shows layers.

6
00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:24.010
And on a roof, slate splits
into thin flat sheets.

7
00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:26.370
Geologists group rocks by how they formed.

8
00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:29.610
So how can a rock tell its story?

9
00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:30.510
Its colour?

10
00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:31.330
Its weight?

11
00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:32.850
How old it looks?

12
00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:35.830
In this mission, you'll
read the clues inside rocks,

13
00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:38.410
and sort them by how they formed.

14
00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:41.430
Then you'll test your
eye on basalt, granite,

15
00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:43.290
sandstone and slate.

16
00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:47.800
Your mission: find out how a rock's
clues reveal how it was formed.
